      "writtenOn": "2025-12-15T20:53:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This should be a `POST` IMHO. The `PUT` verb is for creating resources, whilst the `POST` is for triggering an action.\n\nAlso, the verb should be `flush` rather than `commit`. The data *IS* committed and just waits to be flushed to disk. There is no rollback possible.\n\n\n\n```suggestion\n\u0027PUT /config/server/indexes/link:#index-name[{index-name}]/flush\u0027\n```",
